# privy_roof: Deer Lake's landmark in the research, "a wooden privy roof
# peeking from trees" (BUILD_PLAN S5 brief B5): a small building set down
# among the far shore's firs, so the trees overlap its sides: a bark (10)
# gable over a sliver of bark wall, the eave's shadow on the wall a row of
# ink (0) between them; a forest (12) fir in front of its left end and
# spruce (11) boughs at its right and along its foot, so it never floats
# on the treeline. No door and no lone pixel to read as an eye or a
# light. The anchor, 0,0, is at its foot, the boughs' line. 12 wide, 8
# tall.
C 10  L 4,-7 5,-7  L 3,-6 6,-6  L 2,-5 7,-5  L 1,-4 8,-4
      L 2,-2 7,-2  L 3,-1 7,-1
C 0  L 2,-3 7,-3
C 11  L 8,-3  L 8,-2 9,-2  L 8,-1 9,-1  L 4,0 9,0
C 12  L 0,-5  L -1,-4 0,-4  L -1,-3 0,-3  L -2,-2 0,-2
      L -2,-1 1,-1  L -2,0 3,0
